==Strategy==
This stage will take a while. The different elephant variants work in a surprising synergy to constantly be pushing you back, similar to stages like [[Underground]]. You'll have to use a chip and stall strategy here. Do note that the peon waves are not infinite, meaning you can stall out the peons all the while maintaining the little space you do have here. Any unit that can outrange the elephants (like [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic King Dragon]]) should be used, and the existence of Le'Solar demands a barrier breaker and at LEAST the Crystals from Cats of the Cosmos chapter 1. Do note that you are expected to have a seal level of around 25 by now, so if you struggle here, it would be a good idea to go back and wait for easier stages to be available first.

Units like [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]], consistent shield breakers like [[Li'l Gross Cat (Special Cat)|Talented Li'l Macho Legs]], [[Furiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Furilan Pasilan]] or [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Aku Researcher]] (though unlikely to have at this point) can trivialise the stage due to being incredibly tanky due to the elephants slow attack speeds or able to take ≈2/3rds of Le'Behemoths HP respectively. It's also highly recommended to use some form of nuker like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] to take out the condemned peng quickly. Any other general tankers to slow the progress of the elephants or any units that can consistently knock them back can help considerably including the [[Cat Cannon|Breakerblast Cannon]].

